  "identifier": "simvascular",
  "name": "SimVascular",
  "description": "End-to-end open-source platform for patient-specific cardiovascular blood flow simulation. Provides a complete pipeline from medical image segmentation and vessel lumen extraction, through geometric model construction and finite-element mesh generation, to CFD-based haemodynamic simulation and analysis. Used in cardiovascular surgical planning, device design, and clinical research. Developed at Stanford University and the University of California.",
